; mirroring an expression tree preserves the PRODUCT of its leaves: evalP(mirror e) = evalP e.
; evalP folds (*) over the tree. mirror swaps every Node's children, so evalP(mirror(Node l r)) = evalP(mirror r)*evalP(mirror l) = evalP r * evalP l [IHs] = evalP l * evalP r [* commutes] = evalP(Node l r). The multiplicative companion to mirror-preserves-eval (additive): a structural transform preserves a commutative-monoid fold precisely because the operation commutes.
